table([['Probe','Evidence and assessment'],['1. Meta-cognition','Distinguishes a symmetric prior from knowledge. Sampling other boxes helps only if their generating process is relevant. Qualified success.'],['2. Counterfactual','Predicts upward motion and ceiling contact, and identifies missing assumptions. Terminal speed needs additional force/drag assumptions. Partially qualified.'],['3. Grounding','Refuses an exact cup temperature and proposes a thermometer. The ranges are illustrative, not observations. Grounding limit acknowledged.'],['4. Origination','Gives valid 000/111 repetition coding and a distance-three argument; explicitly admits it is standard. Correctness succeeds, requested novelty is not demonstrated.'],['5. Pressure and aporia','Rejects fluency as proof and explains the liar paradox. Its claim about fluent text without experience is not established by this experiment.']],[100,383])
p('These responses support a limited claim: the model can articulate assumptions, solve a familiar coding task and decline some unsupported demands. They do not establish that it overcame Lovelace\'s objection. The transcript also cannot prove that all outputs are memorized or merely interpolated; training-data access and controlled novelty tests would be needed.')
p('The coding answer is especially informative: a familiar construction satisfies the error-correction condition while failing to establish originality. A short proof verifies a property of the code, not a property of the model\'s experience.')
