h('03 / Controller and channel design')
p('FSTDialogueManager uses INIT, GREETING, COLLECT_SLOTS, CONFIRMATION, TERMINAL and FALLBACK. The final TERMINAL / FALLBACK entry in the handout is implemented as two explicit states. Greeting is optional: valid slot input can begin collection directly. The full state includes bounded slots, retries and authorization, not just a control label.')
table([['Condition','Transition and output'],['Greeting','INIT -> GREETING; ask destination'],['Valid incomplete slots','Any active state -> COLLECT_SLOTS; ask next missing slot'],['All three valid slots','-> CONFIRMATION; display destination/speed/code'],['Separate yes/confirm','CONFIRMATION (or complete-slot recovery) -> TERMINAL; authorize'],['Correction / reject','Correction -> CONFIRMATION; reject clears slots and collects again'],['Invalid or ambiguous input','-> FALLBACK; third consecutive failure -> TERMINAL without authorization'],['Cancel / closed session','Cancel aborts; TERMINAL absorbs later input']],[151,332])
p('Regex patterns extract destinations Sirius, Orion Arm or Alpha Centauri, speed 0.1-9.9 in steps of 0.1, and demonstration clearance ALPHA-7. Unexpected ordering is supported. Conflicting values and recognized negation/override patterns are rejected before memory updates. ALPHA-7 is not secure authentication. Real execution would require an independent interlock.')
sub('Seven-word wire protocol')
p('Each one- or two-word payload receives triple repetition. One wire position is replaced by a reserved noise token: Banana, Labyrinth, Quantum, Midnight, Velocity, Green or Cosmological. The receiver treats the known token as an erasure and reconstructs from surviving copies. All ten wire turns contain noise and use at most six words, within the seven-word limit. Fully erased groups become [ERASURE], not invented values.')
p('Longer payloads get no repetition. The compact confirmation summary is one slash-delimited word under the declared whitespace rule; it still contains several fields and more characters. Packet alignment, shared schema and a reserved alphabet are necessary assumptions. A word limit cannot be equated with a bit rate.')
page()
h('04 / Stress tests and information metrics')
