p('All five expected outcomes passed. The retry mechanism recovers from a valid slot after a bad turn. Terminal sessions cannot be reopened by later commands. Twelve unit tests also cover all six slot orders, missing clearance, correction, invalid values, channel recovery and information identities. These tests do not prove a general natural-language parser safe.')
p('For each coding/noise condition, 4,000 six-word packets use a uniform four-word payload alphabet. Baseline carries six independent words; triple coding carries two repeated words. Exactly k distinct positions are replaced. H(X), H(Y) and I(X;Y) use aligned wire-word counts, in bits per symbol. These pooled marginal estimates are not block-capacity estimates; repetition creates dependence within packets.')
rows=[['Code','k/6','H(X)','H(Y)','I(X;Y)','Recovery']]
for x in r['channel_experiment']:rows.append(['Triple' if x['protected'] else 'Baseline',x['substitutions'],f"{x['H_X']:.3f}",f"{x['H_Y']:.3f}",f"{x['I_XY']:.3f}",f"{100*x['recovered_payload_fraction']:.2f}%"])
table(rows,[90,45,75,75,90,108])
p('Noise increases output entropy while reducing shared information. Repetition improves decoded recovery at a threefold payload cost, rather than increasing per-position mutual information. At three substitutions, whole triples can be erased. Raw conditional entropy values and experiment seeds are in evidence/local_execution.json.')
p('H(X) = -sum p(x) log2 p(x); I(X;Y) = sum p(x,y) log2[p(x,y)/(p(x)p(y))]. For ideal AWGN, C = W log2(1+S/N). At W=1,000 Hz, S/N values 1, 3 and 9 give 1,000, 2,000 and 3,321.93 bits/s. These are illustrative physical capacities, not measured capacities of this word channel. Turn duration and bits per word are unspecified.')
p('Hazards remain: missed negations, unmarked irony, reserved-word collisions and unrecognized substitutions can alter intent. Determinism prevents stochastic state drift, not specification errors. Semantic fidelity and hallucination cannot be inferred from token entropy alone.')
page()
